## Quality Check Rules

**All quality verification is done locally. CI is for build confirmation only.**

### Flow

```
Change area detection (git diff)
    |
Static checks + tests
    |
Review cycles (code changes: 6 personas x 2+ cycles / docs+infra only: reduced personas x 1+ cycle)
    |
E2E tests (final verification)
    |
Report data saved -> .quality-check-passed created -> push allowed
```

### Quality Check Hook

Codex enforces this via a `PreToolUse` hook (configured in `.codex/hooks.json`).
When you run `git push`, Codex checks for `.quality-check-passed`. If missing, the push is blocked.

### Multi-Persona Review

6 specialist personas review in parallel (each spawned with `gpt-5.5` / `model_reasoning_effort = "high"` - see Subagent Model Selection):

| Persona | Focus Area |
|---------|------------|
| Security Engineer | Vulnerabilities, auth, data leaks, injection |
| Software Architect | SOLID/DRY, layer responsibilities, dependencies, extensibility |
| QA Engineer | Edge cases, test coverage, error handling |
| Integration Architecture | Overall consistency, layer dependencies, existing patterns, side effects |
| Performance Engineer | Algorithmic complexity, query performance, bundle size, caching |
| Requirements Consistency Reviewer | Issue/design alignment, acceptance criteria, domain terminology |

- Code changes: minimum 2 cycles. Docs/infra-only changes: reduced persona set, minimum 1 cycle (see `quality-check` skill)
- Repeat until 0 must-fix items
- Run `self-improvement` before creating `.quality-check-passed`

